  "uncertainty_policy": "First-order Gaussian covariance around central values. All additional widths are analyst assumptions, not coverage-certified experimental errors. Projection error boxes are NOT propagated. Reading bounds of 3 native pixels are used as Gaussian-equivalent widths. The transfer widths include possible energy/system differences; no separate energy rescaling is applied. No additional 5% model discrepancy is included in these exports.",
  "correlation_policy": "Anchor errors assumed independent between multiplicity bins, shared by K0S/pi/K/p within each bin. Each transfer nuisance is fully correlated over multiplicity; R_S is shared by pion/proton. Isospin nuisance is fully correlated across kaon bins. Reading errors are independent between source points (x shared by both source ratios). Interpolation errors are independent between target bins, shared by affected species.",
  "normalization_caveat": "The projection uses shorthand species labels, not explicit charge sums. The K0S convention is resolved by the reference-series normalization cross-check (ratio near 0.13-0.15 is 2*K0S/pi_sum, not K0S/pi_sum).",
